{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"tool_srTPj2Us1wwlmm9MEqt7qhKw","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (175KB). Full output saved to: /home/cre/.claude/projects/-data-cre-workspace-se3-0/c746df07-3b5b-47b3-9b75-8570058f7780/tool-results/bfb44ed.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n# Manager Agent Rules\n\nYou are a MANAGER agent in an SE3 git-worktree collaboration session.\nYou are invoked on-demand by the orchestrator to make decisions. You are NOT resident — you read state from `.collab/`, decide, output JSON, and exit.\n\n## Your Scope\n\nYou handle strategic decisions. You do NOT:\n- Write implementation code\n- Run tests directly\n- Manage git worktrees or branches (the orchestrator does this)\n- Interact with users directly (use `ask_human` MCP tool if needed)\n\n## Decision Types\n\nYou respond to events with ONE of these actions:\n\n| Action | When to Use |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `plan` | Initial task decomposition. Break the objective into parallel tasks. |\n| `merge` | Worker completed, code looks good. Approve the merge. |\n| `reject` | Worker completed, but code has issues. Provide specific feedback. |\n| `retry` | Worker failed, but the task is retryable. Provide adjusted guidance. |\n| `split` | Task is too large or complex. Break it into smaller sub-tasks. |\n| `escalate` | You cannot resolve the issue. Route to human. |\n| `complete` | All tasks are merged and the objective is fulfilled. |\n\n## Response Format\n\nYou MUST respond with valid JSON only. No markdown, no explanation outside JSON.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"plan|merge|reject|retry|split|escalate|complete\",\n  \"tasks\": [],\n  \"target_task\": \"task-id\",\n  \"merge_branch\": \"branch-name\",\n  \"retry_prompt\": \"adjusted prompt\",\n  \"reason\": \"explanation\",\n  \"summary\": \"human-readable summary\"\n}\n```\n\n## Task Decomposition Rules (for `plan` action)\n\n1. **Maximize parallelism**: Tasks that touch different files/modules should be separate\n2. **Minimize dependencies**: If task B depends on task A's output, note this — the orchestrator merges A first\n3. **Bounded scope**: Each task should be completable in one session (< 60 minutes)\n4. **Clear spec references**: Each task must reference the spec files the worker needs to read\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c746df07-3b5b-47b3-9b75-8570058f7780","uuid":"b2fca1c3-d60b-4372-a579-45bbaa48ddb8","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Manager Agent Rules\n\nYou are a MANAGER agent in an SE3 git-worktree collaboration session.\nYou are invoked on-demand by the orchestrator to make decisions. You are NOT resident — you read state from `.collab/`, decide, output JSON, and exit.\n\n## Your Scope\n\nYou handle strategic decisions. You do NOT:\n- Write implementation code\n- Run tests directly\n- Manage git worktrees or branches (the orchestrator does this)\n- Interact with users directly (use `ask_human` MCP tool if needed)\n\n## Decision Types\n\nYou respond to events with ONE of these actions:\n\n| Action | When to Use |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `plan` | Initial task decomposition. Break the objective into parallel tasks. |\n| `merge` | Worker completed, code looks good. Approve the merge. |\n| `reject` | Worker completed, but code has issues. Provide specific feedback. |\n| `retry` | Worker failed, but the task is retryable. Provide adjusted guidance. |\n| `split` | Task is too large or complex. Break it into smaller sub-tasks. |\n| `escalate` | You cannot resolve the issue. Route to human. |\n| `complete` | All tasks are merged and the objective is fulfilled. |\n\n## Response Format\n\nYou MUST respond with valid JSON only. No markdown, no explanation outside JSON.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"plan|merge|reject|retry|split|escalate|complete\",\n  \"tasks\": [],\n  \"target_task\": \"task-id\",\n  \"merge_branch\": \"branch-name\",\n  \"retry_prompt\": \"adjusted prompt\",\n  \"reason\": \"explanation\",\n  \"summary\": \"human-readable summary\"\n}\n```\n\n## Task Decomposition Rules (for `plan` action)\n\n1. **Maximize parallelism**: Tasks that touch different files/modules should be separate\n2. **Minimize dependencies**: If task B depends on task A's output, note this — the orchestrator merges A first\n3. **Bounded scope**: Each task should be completable in one session (< 60 minutes)\n4. **Clear spec references**: Each task must reference the spec files the worker needs to read\n5. **Self-contained prompts**: The worker has NO context beyond the prompt you write and the files in its worktree. Include everything it needs.\n\n### Task Definition Format\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"task-001\",\n  \"branch\": \"collab/short-description\",\n  \"worktree\": \".worktrees/short-description\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"title\": \"Human-readable title\",\n  \"prompt\": \"Full, detailed prompt for the worker. Include: what to implement, which files to read, which specs to follow, what tests to write.\",\n  \"spec_refs\": [\"openspec/specs/relevant-spec/spec.md\"],\n  \"dependencies\": [],\n  \"health\": {\n    \"timeout_minutes\": 60,\n    \"attempts\": 0,\n    \"max_attempts\": 3\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Code Review Rules (for `merge` / `reject` decisions)\n\nWhen reviewing a completed worker's branch:\n\n1. **Check the diff summary** — does it match the task scope? No unrelated changes?\n2. **Check test results** — did the worker run and pass tests?\n3. **Check spec compliance** — does the implementation satisfy the spec scenarios?\n4. **Check for regressions** — any obvious issues in the diff?\n\nApprove (`merge`) unless there are clear problems. Don't reject for style nitpicks.\nReject (`reject`) with specific, actionable feedback the worker can act on.\n\n## Failure Handling Rules\n\n- **Timeout**: If the worker timed out, consider: Was the task too large? → `split`. Was the prompt unclear? → `retry` with better prompt. Repeated timeout? → `escalate`.\n- **Error exit**: Read the worker log. Identify the root cause. If fixable by retry with guidance → `retry`. If systemic → `escalate`.\n- **Blocked**: Worker couldn't proceed without information. Can you answer from context? If yes → `retry` with the answer included in prompt. If no → `escalate` to human.\n\n## Merge Order\n\nWhen multiple branches are ready for merge:\n1. Foundational/infrastructure changes first\n2. Changes that other tasks depend on\n3. Independent feature changes (any order)\n4. Changes that modify the same files as already-merged branches go LAST (higher conflict risk)\n\n## MCP Tools Available\n\n- **ask_human(question, options?, urgent?)** — Escalate to human when you cannot make a decision. Use sparingly.\n- **notify_human(message, level)** — Inform human of significant events (all tasks done, critical failure, etc.)\n\n## What NOT to Do\n\n- Do NOT guess when unsure — use `escalate`\n- Do NOT approve merges without reviewing the diff summary\n- Do NOT create tasks with vague prompts — workers have zero context beyond what you write\n- Do NOT retry indefinitely — respect max_attempts\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\nProject root: /data/cre/workspace/se3.0\nBase branch: master\n\n## All Tasks\nnull\n{\"id\": \"task-002\", \"branch\": \"collab/verify-human-calls-archive\", \"worktree\": \".worktrees/verify-human-calls-archive\", \"status\": \"in_progress\", \"title\": \"Verify human calls archiving system\", \"prompt\": \"Verify that the human calls archiving system is fully functional. Check the se3 human-calls archive and se3 human-calls list commands. Verify that completed calls are properly archived.\", \"spec_refs\": [], \"dependencies\": [], \"health\": {\"timeout_minutes\": 30, \"attempts\": 1, \"max_attempts\": 2, \"last_activity\": \"2026-02-18T21:46:37.842596\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-02-18T20:35:27\", \"started_at\": \"now\", \"worker_pid\": 2527908}\n\n\n## Event\nType: failure\nContext:\nTask task-001 failed with exit code 1.\n\nWorker log (last 50 lines):\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"tool_17tx5v5YplWsSNst8VWWpphM\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"     1→\\\"\\\"\\\"Tests for the openspec CLI commands.\\n     2→\\n     3→Tests cover:\\n     4→- openspec init: Initialize the openspec/ directory structure\\n     5→- openspec list --specs: List all available specs\\n     6→\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     7→\\n     8→import json\\n     9→import os\\n    10→import sys\\n    11→import tempfile\\n    12→from pathlib import Path\\n    13→from unittest.mock import patch, MagicMock\\n    14→\\n    15→import pytest\\n    16→\\n    17→# Add tools to path for imports\\n    18→sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).parent.parent / \\\"tools\\\"))\\n    19→\\n    20→from se3_tools.commands.openspec import initialize_openspec, list_specs\\n    21→\\n    22→\\n    23→# =============================================================================\\n    24→# OpenSpec Init Tests\\n    25→# =============================================================================\\n    26→\\n    27→class TestOpenSpecInit:\\n    28→    \\\"\\\"\\\"Test openspec init command.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    29→\\n    30→    def setup_method(self):\\n    31→        self.tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\\n    32→        self.project_root = Path(self.tmpdir)\\n    33→\\n    34→    def test_initialize_openspec_creates_directories(self):\\n    35→        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec init should create openspec/, specs/, changes/, changes/archive/.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    36→        result = initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\\n    37→\\n    38→        assert result[\\\"success\\\"] is True\\n    39→        assert len(result[\\\"created\\\"]) == 3\\n    40→        assert len(result[\\\"existing\\\"]) == 0\\n    41→\\n    42→        # Verify directories exist\\n    43→        assert (self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"specs\\\").exists()\\n    44→        assert (self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"changes\\\").exists()\\n    45→        assert (self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"changes\\\" / \\\"archive\\\").exists()\\n    46→\\n    47→    def test_initialize_openspec_idempotent(self):\\n    48→        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec init should be idempotent - not fail if run twice.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    49→        # First init\\n    50→        result1 = initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\\n    51→        assert result1[\\\"success\\\"] is True\\n    52→        assert len(result1[\\\"created\\\"]) == 3\\n    53→\\n    54→        # Second init without force\\n    55→        result2 = initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\\n    56→        assert result2[\\\"success\\\"] is True\\n    57→        assert len(result2[\\\"existing\\\"]) == 3\\n    58→        assert \\\"already initialized\\\" in result2[\\\"message\\\"].lower()\\n    59→\\n    60→    def test_initialize_openspec_with_force(self):\\n    61→        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec init --force should reinitialize even if exists.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    62→        # First init\\n    63→        initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\\n    64→\\n    65→        # Force reinit\\n    66→        result = initialize_openspec(self.project_root, force=True)\\n    67→        assert result[\\\"success\\\"] is True\\n    68→        # With force, it still reports existing since directories already exist\\n    69→        assert len(result[\\\"existing\\\"]) == 3\\n    70→\\n    71→\\n    72→# =============================================================================\\n    73→# OpenSpec List Tests\\n    74→# =============================================================================\\n    75→\\n    76→class TestOpenSpecList:\\n    77→    \\\"\\\"\\\"Test openspec list --specs command.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    78→\\n    79→    def setup_method(self):\\n    80→        self.tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\\n    81→        self.project_root = Path(self.tmpdir)\\n    82→\\n    83→        # Create openspec structure\\n    84→        self.specs_dir = self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"specs\\\"\\n    85→        self.specs_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\\n    86→\\n    87→    def _create_spec(self, name: str, purpose: str = None):\\n    88→        \\\"\\\"\\\"Helper to create a spec file.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    89→        spec_dir = self.specs_dir / name\\n    90→        spec_dir.mkdir()\\n    91→\\n    92→        content = f\\\"# {name} Specification\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n    93→        content += \\\"## Purpose\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n    94→        if purpose:\\n    95→            content += f\\\"{purpose}\\\\n\\\"\\n    96→        content += \\\"\\\\n## Requirements\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n    97→        content += \\\"### Requirement: Test\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n    98→        content += \\\"The system SHALL test.\\\\n\\\"\\n    99→\\n   100→        spec_file = spec_dir / \\\"spec.md\\\"\\n   101→        spec_file.write_text(content)\\n   102→        return spec_file\\n   103→\\n   104→    def test_list_specs_empty(self):\\n   105→        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec list --specs should return empty list when no specs.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   106→        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\\n   107→        assert specs == []\\n   108→\\n   109→    def test_list_specs_single(self):\\n   110→        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec list --specs should list a single spec.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   111→        self._create_spec(\\\"test-spec\\\", \\\"Test purpose description\\\")\\n   112→\\n   113→        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\\n   114→        assert len(specs) == 1\\n   115→        assert specs[0][\\\"name\\\"] == \\\"test-spec\\\"\\n   116→        assert \\\"openspec/specs/test-spec/spec.md\\\" in specs[0][\\\"path\\\"]\\n   117→        assert \\\"Test purpose\\\" in specs[0][\\\"purpose\\\"]\\n   118→\\n   119→    def test_list_specs_multiple(self):\\n   120→        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec list --specs should list multiple specs sorted by name.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   121→        self._create_spec(\\\"zebra-spec\\\", \\\"Zebra spec purpose\\\")\\n   122→        self._create_spec(\\\"alpha-spec\\\", \\\"Alpha spec purpose\\\")\\n   123→        self._create_spec(\\\"beta-spec\\\", \\\"Beta spec purpose\\\")\\n   124→\\n   125→        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\\n   126→        assert len(specs) == 3\\n   127→\\n   128→        # Should be sorted alphabetically\\n   129→        assert specs[0][\\\"name\\\"] == \\\"alpha-spec\\\"\\n   130→        assert specs[1][\\\"name\\\"] == \\\"beta-spec\\\"\\n   131→        assert specs[2][\\\"name\\\"] == \\\"zebra-spec\\\"\\n   132→\\n   133→    def test_list_specs_ignores_non_spec_dirs(self):\\n   134→        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec list --specs should ignore directories without spec.md.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   135→        # Create a spec\\n   136→        self._create_spec(\\\"valid-spec\\\", \\\"Valid spec\\\")\\n   137→\\n   138→        # Create a directory without spec.md\\n   139→        (self.specs_dir / \\\"empty-dir\\\").mkdir()\\n   140→\\n   141→        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\\n   142→        assert len(specs) == 1\\n   143→        assert specs[0][\\\"name\\\"] == \\\"valid-spec\\\"\\n   144→\\n   145→    def test_list_specs_no_openspec_dir(self):\\n   146→        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec list --specs should handle missing openspec directory.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   147→        # Remove openspec directory\\n   148→        import shutil\\n   149→        shutil.rmtree(self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\")\\n   150→\\n   151→        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\\n   152→        assert specs == []\\n   153→\\n   154→\\n   155→# =============================================================================\\n   156→# CLI Integration Tests\\n   157→# =============================================================================\\n   158→\\n   159→class TestOpenSpecCLI:\\n   160→    \\\"\\\"\\\"Test openspec CLI commands via typer.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   161→\\n   162→    def setup_method(self):\\n   163→        self.tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\\n   164→        self.project_root = Path(self.tmpdir)\\n   165→\\n   166→    def test_cli_init_command(self):\\n   167→        \\\"\\\"\\\"Test the CLI init command directly.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   168→        from typer.testing import CliRunner\\n   169→        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\\n   170→\\n   171→        runner = CliRunner()\\n   172→        result = runner.invoke(app, [\\\"init\\\", \\\"--project-root\\\", str(self.project_root)])\\n   173→\\n   174→        assert result.exit_code == 0\\n   175→        assert \\\"Created directories\\\" in result.output\\n   176→\\n   177→        # Verify directories exist\\n   178→        assert (self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"specs\\\").exists()\\n   179→\\n   180→    def test_cli_list_specs_command(self):\\n   181→        \\\"\\\"\\\"Test the CLI list --specs command.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   182→        from typer.testing import CliRunner\\n   183→        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\\n   184→\\n   185→        # Create a spec\\n   186→        specs_dir = self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"specs\\\"\\n   187→        specs_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\\n   188→        spec_dir = specs_dir / \\\"test-spec\\\"\\n   189→        spec_dir.mkdir()\\n   190→        spec_file = spec_dir / \\\"spec.md\\\"\\n   191→        spec_file.write_text(\\\"# Test Spec\\\\n\\\\n## Purpose\\\\n\\\\nTest purpose.\\\\n\\\")\\n   192→\\n   193→        runner = CliRunner()\\n   194→        result = runner.invoke(app, [\\\"list\\\", \\\"--specs\\\", \\\"--project-root\\\", str(self.project_root)])\\n   195→\\n   196→        assert result.exit_code == 0\\n   197→        assert \\\"test-spec\\\" in result.output\\n   198→        assert \\\"Test purpose\\\" in result.output\\n   199→\\n   200→    def test_cli_list_specs_json_format(self):\\n   201→        \\\"\\\"\\\"Test the CLI list --specs --format json command.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   202→        from typer.testing import CliRunner\\n   203→        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\\n   204→\\n   205→        # Create a spec\\n   206→        specs_dir = self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"specs\\\"\\n   207→        specs_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\\n   208→        spec_dir = specs_dir / \\\"test-spec\\\"\\n   209→        spec_dir.mkdir()\\n   210→        spec_file = spec_dir / \\\"spec.md\\\"\\n   211→        spec_file.write_text(\\\"# Test Spec\\\\n\\\\n## Purpose\\\\n\\\\nTest purpose.\\\\n\\\")\\n   212→\\n   213→        runner = CliRunner()\\n   214→        result = runner.invoke(app, [\\\"list\\\", \\\"--specs\\\", \\\"--project-root\\\", str(self.project_root), \\\"--format\\\", \\\"json\\\"])\\n   215→\\n   216→        assert result.exit_code == 0\\n   217→        data = json.loads(result.output)\\n   218→        assert len(data) == 1\\n   219→        assert data[0][\\\"name\\\"] == \\\"test-spec\\\"\\n   220→\\n   221→    def test_cli_init_json_format(self):\\n   222→        \\\"\\\"\\\"Test the CLI init --format json command.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n   223→        from typer.testing import CliRunner\\n   224→        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\\n   225→\\n   226→        runner = CliRunner()\\n   227→        result = runner.invoke(app, [\\\"init\\\", \\\"--project-root\\\", str(self.project_root), \\\"--format\\\", \\\"json\\\"])\\n   228→\\n   229→        assert result.exit_code == 0\\n   230→        data = json.loads(result.output)\\n   231→        assert data[\\\"success\\\"] is True\\n   232→        assert len(data[\\\"created\\\"]) == 3\\n   233→\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"e569dacb-b70b-4c90-930f-0ca840cf5264\",\"uuid\":\"61bffdb3-438d-4431-a4f2-f60adf339d45\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/data/cre/workspace/se3.0/.worktrees/verify-openspec-commands/tests/test_openspec.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Tests for the openspec CLI commands.\\n\\nTests cover:\\n- openspec init: Initialize the openspec/ directory structure\\n- openspec list --specs: List all available specs\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nimport tempfile\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom unittest.mock import patch, MagicMock\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\n# Add tools to path for imports\\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).parent.parent / \\\"tools\\\"))\\n\\nfrom se3_tools.commands.openspec import initialize_openspec, list_specs\\n\\n\\n# =============================================================================\\n# OpenSpec Init Tests\\n# =============================================================================\\n\\nclass TestOpenSpecInit:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Test openspec init command.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def setup_method(self):\\n        self.tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\\n        self.project_root = Path(self.tmpdir)\\n\\n    def test_initialize_openspec_creates_directories(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec init should create openspec/, specs/, changes/, changes/archive/.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        result = initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\\n\\n        assert result[\\\"success\\\"] is True\\n        assert len(result[\\\"created\\\"]) == 3\\n        assert len(result[\\\"existing\\\"]) == 0\\n\\n        # Verify directories exist\\n        assert (self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"specs\\\").exists()\\n        assert (self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"changes\\\").exists()\\n        assert (self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"changes\\\" / \\\"archive\\\").exists()\\n\\n    def test_initialize_openspec_idempotent(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec init should be idempotent - not fail if run twice.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        # First init\\n        result1 = initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\\n        assert result1[\\\"success\\\"] is True\\n        assert len(result1[\\\"created\\\"]) == 3\\n\\n        # Second init without force\\n        result2 = initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\\n        assert result2[\\\"success\\\"] is True\\n        assert len(result2[\\\"existing\\\"]) == 3\\n        assert \\\"already initialized\\\" in result2[\\\"message\\\"].lower()\\n\\n    def test_initialize_openspec_with_force(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec init --force should reinitialize even if exists.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        # First init\\n        initialize_openspec(self.project_root)\\n\\n        # Force reinit\\n        result = initialize_openspec(self.project_root, force=True)\\n        assert result[\\\"success\\\"] is True\\n        # With force, it still reports existing since directories already exist\\n        assert len(result[\\\"existing\\\"]) == 3\\n\\n\\n# =============================================================================\\n# OpenSpec List Tests\\n# =============================================================================\\n\\nclass TestOpenSpecList:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Test openspec list --specs command.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def setup_method(self):\\n        self.tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\\n        self.project_root = Path(self.tmpdir)\\n\\n        # Create openspec structure\\n        self.specs_dir = self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"specs\\\"\\n        self.specs_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\\n\\n    def _create_spec(self, name: str, purpose: str = None):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Helper to create a spec file.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        spec_dir = self.specs_dir / name\\n        spec_dir.mkdir()\\n\\n        content = f\\\"# {name} Specification\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n        content += \\\"## Purpose\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n        if purpose:\\n            content += f\\\"{purpose}\\\\n\\\"\\n        content += \\\"\\\\n## Requirements\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n        content += \\\"### Requirement: Test\\\\n\\\\n\\\"\\n        content += \\\"The system SHALL test.\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n        spec_file = spec_dir / \\\"spec.md\\\"\\n        spec_file.write_text(content)\\n        return spec_file\\n\\n    def test_list_specs_empty(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec list --specs should return empty list when no specs.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\\n        assert specs == []\\n\\n    def test_list_specs_single(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec list --specs should list a single spec.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self._create_spec(\\\"test-spec\\\", \\\"Test purpose description\\\")\\n\\n        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\\n        assert len(specs) == 1\\n        assert specs[0][\\\"name\\\"] == \\\"test-spec\\\"\\n        assert \\\"openspec/specs/test-spec/spec.md\\\" in specs[0][\\\"path\\\"]\\n        assert \\\"Test purpose\\\" in specs[0][\\\"purpose\\\"]\\n\\n    def test_list_specs_multiple(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec list --specs should list multiple specs sorted by name.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        self._create_spec(\\\"zebra-spec\\\", \\\"Zebra spec purpose\\\")\\n        self._create_spec(\\\"alpha-spec\\\", \\\"Alpha spec purpose\\\")\\n        self._create_spec(\\\"beta-spec\\\", \\\"Beta spec purpose\\\")\\n\\n        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\\n        assert len(specs) == 3\\n\\n        # Should be sorted alphabetically\\n        assert specs[0][\\\"name\\\"] == \\\"alpha-spec\\\"\\n        assert specs[1][\\\"name\\\"] == \\\"beta-spec\\\"\\n        assert specs[2][\\\"name\\\"] == \\\"zebra-spec\\\"\\n\\n    def test_list_specs_ignores_non_spec_dirs(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec list --specs should ignore directories without spec.md.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        # Create a spec\\n        self._create_spec(\\\"valid-spec\\\", \\\"Valid spec\\\")\\n\\n        # Create a directory without spec.md\\n        (self.specs_dir / \\\"empty-dir\\\").mkdir()\\n\\n        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\\n        assert len(specs) == 1\\n        assert specs[0][\\\"name\\\"] == \\\"valid-spec\\\"\\n\\n    def test_list_specs_no_openspec_dir(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"openspec list --specs should handle missing openspec directory.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        # Remove openspec directory\\n        import shutil\\n        shutil.rmtree(self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\")\\n\\n        specs = list_specs(self.project_root)\\n        assert specs == []\\n\\n\\n# =============================================================================\\n# CLI Integration Tests\\n# =============================================================================\\n\\nclass TestOpenSpecCLI:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Test openspec CLI commands via typer.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def setup_method(self):\\n        self.tmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\\n        self.project_root = Path(self.tmpdir)\\n\\n    def test_cli_init_command(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Test the CLI init command directly.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        from typer.testing import CliRunner\\n        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\\n\\n        runner = CliRunner()\\n        result = runner.invoke(app, [\\\"init\\\", \\\"--project-root\\\", str(self.project_root)])\\n\\n        assert result.exit_code == 0\\n        assert \\\"Created directories\\\" in result.output\\n\\n        # Verify directories exist\\n        assert (self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"specs\\\").exists()\\n\\n    def test_cli_list_specs_command(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Test the CLI list --specs command.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        from typer.testing import CliRunner\\n        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\\n\\n        # Create a spec\\n        specs_dir = self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"specs\\\"\\n        specs_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\\n        spec_dir = specs_dir / \\\"test-spec\\\"\\n        spec_dir.mkdir()\\n        spec_file = spec_dir / \\\"spec.md\\\"\\n        spec_file.write_text(\\\"# Test Spec\\\\n\\\\n## Purpose\\\\n\\\\nTest purpose.\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n        runner = CliRunner()\\n        result = runner.invoke(app, [\\\"list\\\", \\\"--specs\\\", \\\"--project-root\\\", str(self.project_root)])\\n\\n        assert result.exit_code == 0\\n        assert \\\"test-spec\\\" in result.output\\n        assert \\\"Test purpose\\\" in result.output\\n\\n    def test_cli_list_specs_json_format(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Test the CLI list --specs --format json command.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        from typer.testing import CliRunner\\n        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\\n\\n        # Create a spec\\n        specs_dir = self.project_root / \\\"openspec\\\" / \\\"specs\\\"\\n        specs_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\\n        spec_dir = specs_dir / \\\"test-spec\\\"\\n        spec_dir.mkdir()\\n        spec_file = spec_dir / \\\"spec.md\\\"\\n        spec_file.write_text(\\\"# Test Spec\\\\n\\\\n## Purpose\\\\n\\\\nTest purpose.\\\\n\\\")\\n\\n        runner = CliRunner()\\n        result = runner.invoke(app, [\\\"list\\\", \\\"--specs\\\", \\\"--project-root\\\", str(self.project_root), \\\"--format\\\", \\\"json\\\"])\\n\\n        assert result.exit_code == 0\\n        data = json.loads(result.output)\\n        assert len(data) == 1\\n        assert data[0][\\\"name\\\"] == \\\"test-spec\\\"\\n\\n    def test_cli_init_json_format(self):\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Test the CLI init --format json command.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        from typer.testing import CliRunner\\n        from se3_tools.commands.openspec import app\\n\\n        runner = CliRunner()\\n        result = runner.invoke(app, [\\\"init\\\", \\\"--project-root\\\", str(self.project_root), \\\"--format\\\", \\\"json\\\"])\\n\\n        assert result.exit_code == 0\\n        data = json.loads(result.output)\\n        assert data[\\\"success\\\"] is True\\n        assert len(data[\\\"created\\\"]) == 3\\n\",\"numLines\":233,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":233}}}\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"msg_xev57YOokoA90L41djuFiWl